        "math_academy_id": "q-161685",
        "problem": "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xz$-plane and the surface $y=5-3{z}^{2},$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=1,$ $z=-1,$ $z=0.$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le z\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5-3{z}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={\u222d}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{5-3{z}^{2}}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[y]_{y=0}^{y=5-3{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}5-3{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[5z-{z}^{3}]_{z=-1}^{z=0}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}0-(5(-1)-(-1)^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5-1\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}dx \\\\  & =4[x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
